   $q$Read the sentences: "The museum opened in 1998. The museum displays six working printing presses. The museum offers weekly demonstrations." Which revision best varies the sentence structure while keeping every fact?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The museum opened in 1998. The museum displays six working printing presses and offers weekly demonstrations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repetitive-openings"},{"text":"Opened in 1998, the museum displays six working printing presses and offers weekly demonstrations.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The museum opened in 1998, the museum displays six printing presses, the museum offers demonstrations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"Opened in 1998, the museum displays six working printing presses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Opened in 1998, the museum displays six working printing presses and offers weekly demonstrations.$q$, $q$The opening participial phrase and the compound verb remove the repeated "The museum" and keep all three facts. The choice "Opened in 1998, the museum displays six working printing presses" varies the structure too, but it leaves out the weekly demonstrations.$q$, 'draft', null)
