   $q$Read the sentence: "The committee utilized a methodology of a quantitative nature in order to ascertain levels of attendance." Which revision is the clearest while staying formal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The committee used interviews to explain why attendance fell.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"The committee utilized quantitative methodologies so as to ascertain attendance levels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inflated-diction"},{"text":"The committee used quantitative methods to measure attendance.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The committee just counted up how many folks showed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The committee used quantitative methods to measure attendance.$q$, $q$Plain formal words like "used," "methods," and "measure" say the same thing without the inflated phrasing. The choice with "quantitative methodologies" is a little shorter but keeps the pompous "utilized" and "ascertain."$q$, 'draft', null)
