   $q$Read the sentence from a formal essay: "One should verify sources before you cite them in a paper." Which revision keeps a consistent formal point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"You should verify sources before one cites them in a paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifting-pov"},{"text":"One should verify sources after citing them in a paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"One should verify sources before citing them in a paper.","is_correct":true},{"text":"One should verify sources before you go and cite them in a paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifting-pov"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One should verify sources before citing them in a paper.$q$, $q$Changing "you cite them" to "citing them" removes the shift from "one" to "you." The choice "You should verify sources before one cites them" simply reverses the shift, so the pronouns still clash.$q$, 'draft', null)
