   $q$Read the sentences: "The fencing club meets on Tuesdays. Because the gym is reserved for basketball the rest of the week." What is the problem with the second group of words?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a fused sentence with no punctuation between two clauses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-fragment-with-fused"},{"text":"It is a fragment: a dependent clause punctuated as if it were a sentence.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It has no problem and can stand correctly on its own as a sentence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-unrecognized"},{"text":"It is a comma splice that joins two independent clauses with a comma.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-error-type"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a fragment: a dependent clause punctuated as if it were a sentence.$q$, $q$"Because" makes the clause dependent, so it cannot stand alone and is a fragment. It is not a comma splice or a fused sentence, since it contains only one clause and no comma joining clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
