   $q$Read the sentences: "The cartographers surveyed the coastline by kayak. They wanted to record inlets that aerial photographs had missed." Which choice combines the sentences most clearly and correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The cartographers surveyed the coastline by kayak. Wanting to record inlets that aerial photographs had missed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"The cartographers surveyed the coastline by kayak to record inlets that aerial photographs had missed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The cartographers surveyed the coastline by kayak, they wanted to record inlets that aerial photographs had missed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The cartographers surveyed the coastline by kayak, although they wanted to record inlets that aerial photographs had missed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"illogical-connector"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The cartographers surveyed the coastline by kayak to record inlets that aerial photographs had missed.$q$, $q$The infinitive "to record" shows the purpose of the kayak survey in one complete sentence. "Although" suggests a contrast, but recording missed inlets is the reason for the survey, not something opposed to it.$q$, 'draft', null)
