   $q$Which choice is a fused sentence (two independent clauses run together with no punctuation)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The weather balloon rose nearly twenty miles, where its instruments recorded temperatures far below zero.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"relative-clause-misread"},{"text":"The weather balloon rose nearly twenty miles its instruments recorded temperatures far below zero.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The weather balloon rose nearly twenty miles; its instruments recorded temperatures far below zero.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misread"},{"text":"As the weather balloon rose nearly twenty miles, its instruments recorded temperatures far below zero.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"complex-sentence-misread"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The weather balloon rose nearly twenty miles its instruments recorded temperatures far below zero.$q$, $q$"The weather balloon rose" and "its instruments recorded" are independent clauses with nothing between them, so the sentence is fused. The semicolon version correctly separates the same two clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
