   $q$Which choice is a fragment even though it is long and detailed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Among the volunteers at the wildlife rehabilitation center, a retired veterinarian who trained new staff to feed orphaned owls.","is_correct":true},{"text":"At the wildlife rehabilitation center, a retired veterinarian trained new staff, who then fed the orphaned owls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"relative-clause-misread"},{"text":"Among the volunteers at the wildlife rehabilitation center was a retired veterinarian who trained new staff to feed orphaned owls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-sentence-misread"},{"text":"Training new staff to feed orphaned owls was the main job of a retired veterinarian at the wildlife rehabilitation center.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gerund-subject-misread-as-fragment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Among the volunteers at the wildlife rehabilitation center, a retired veterinarian who trained new staff to feed orphaned owls.$q$, $q$In the fragment, "trained" belongs to the "who" clause, so "veterinarian" has no main verb. The choice with "was" is a complete inverted sentence whose subject "veterinarian" follows the verb "was."$q$, 'draft', null)
