   $q$Read the sentence: "The museum's lead conservator, who had studied the painter's letters for months, insisting that the varnish be removed from only one corner at a time." Which revision fixes the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The museum's lead conservator, who had studied the painter's letters for months, insisted that the varnish be removed from only one corner at a time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The museum's lead conservator had studied the painter's letters for months, the conservator then insisted that the varnish be removed from only one corner at a time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The museum's lead conservator, who had studied the painter's letters for months; insisting that the varnish be removed from only one corner at a time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"},{"text":"The museum's lead conservator, who had studied the painter's letters for months and insisting that the varnish be removed from only one corner at a time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-unfixed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The museum's lead conservator, who had studied the painter's letters for months, insisted that the varnish be removed from only one corner at a time.$q$, $q$The subject "conservator" needs a main verb, and changing "insisting" to "insisted" supplies one. Rewriting it as two clauses joined by a comma fixes the fragment but creates a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
