   $q$A peer suggests deleting sentence 8 because it does not quote the story. Which response best explains what the writer should do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keep it, because it explains the author's choice that makes the comparison of sentences 3 and 7 meaningful.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Keep it, because it adds new plot information about the cold snap and the church.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"Delete it, because an analysis of a story should be built only from direct quotations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misunderstands-analysis"},{"text":"Delete it, because it repeats the plot event already described in sentence 6.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-repetition"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keep it, because it explains the author's choice that makes the comparison of sentences 3 and 7 meaningful.$q$, $q$Sentence 8 is analysis: it points out that returning Teodor to the same piano is a deliberate structural choice that sets up the comparison. Sentence 6 reports the event, but sentence 8 explains why it matters, so it is not a repetition.$q$, 'draft', 'ed20a3a4-dd83-52e9-ae1c-07011d2f86b0')
