   $q$Which sentence should be deleted because it does not support the writer's analysis of the study?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 3, because it describes what the researchers expected rather than what they found.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-needed-context"},{"text":"Sentence 10, because pointing out limits in the study weakens the writer's claim.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"avoids-counterclaim"},{"text":"Sentence 6, because the exact distances are too detailed for a short response.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"},{"text":"Sentence 11, because how dragonflies hunt has nothing to do with how they migrate.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 11, because how dragonflies hunt has nothing to do with how they migrate.$q$, $q$Sentence 11 is about hunting, not about how wind shapes migration. Sentence 10 should stay, because naming the study's limits makes the writer's careful conclusion more believable.$q$, 'draft', 'cb089783-aab3-5f17-8e7f-a0da3a07aa3b')
