   $q$Why is the comparison in sentence 6 stronger evidence for the writer's claim than sentence 4 alone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that dragonflies cannot travel at all unless a strong wind is blowing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"It gives exact numbers, and numbers are always more convincing than a description.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"numbers-equal-proof"},{"text":"It links the long bursts to wind conditions, showing a cause rather than just a travel pattern.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that calm days are more common than windy days during the autumn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It links the long bursts to wind conditions, showing a cause rather than just a travel pattern.$q$, $q$Sentence 4 only describes resting and then flying far; sentence 6 shows the long flights happen on north wind days, which connects the pattern to the wind. The insects still moved a little on calm days, so the data do not show they cannot travel without wind.$q$, 'draft', 'cb089783-aab3-5f17-8e7f-a0da3a07aa3b')
