  ('27bb35b9-06f7-52f6-aaf6-e2d19f8e355a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'data-statistics'), null, 'hard',
   $q$What is the population standard deviation of the data set 2, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 7, 9?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$32$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-divide-by-count"},{"text":"$4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-square-root"},{"text":"$1.5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"computed-mean-absolute-deviation"},{"text":"$2$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$2$$q$, $q$The mean is $\frac{40}{8} = 5$. The squared deviations are $9, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 4, 16$, which add to $32$. Divide by 8 to get the variance, $4$, then take the square root: $\sqrt{4} = 2$. The value $4$ is the variance; the standard deviation needs the square root.$q$, 'draft', null)
