  ('2977a3b5-aae2-505b-9041-67385529330d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'data-statistics'), null, 'medium',
   $q$A data set is strongly skewed to the right, with a long tail of large values, and its mean is 48. Which statement about its median is most likely true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The median is equal to 48.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-mean-equals-median"},{"text":"Nothing can be said about the median without the data.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-shape-gives-no-information"},{"text":"The median is less than 48.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The median is greater than 48.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-skew-direction"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The median is less than 48.$q$, $q$In a right-skewed distribution, the few large values in the tail pull the mean up, while the median stays with the bulk of the data. So the median is most likely less than the mean of $48$. The mean and median are equal only for a symmetric distribution.$q$, 'draft', null)
