  ('6a4057b9-b78d-5ac1-98d1-6a19e7629c5a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'data-statistics'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Two lab groups timed a reaction, in seconds. Group A recorded 12, 15, 18, 15 and Group B recorded 10, 20, 14, 16. Which statement compares the groups correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The groups have the same mean, and Group A's times are more spread out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-spread-comparison"},{"text":"The groups have the same mean and the same spread.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-spread"},{"text":"Group A has the greater mean.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"miscalculated-mean"},{"text":"The groups have the same mean, and Group B's times are more spread out.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The groups have the same mean, and Group B's times are more spread out.$q$, $q$Both sums are $60$, so both means are $\frac{60}{4} = 15$. Group A's times run from $12$ to $18$, a range of $6$, while Group B's run from $10$ to $20$, a range of $10$, and Group B's values sit farther from $15$. Equal means do not mean equal spread.$q$, 'draft', null)
